@@ -70,6 +70,15 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` and :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. It writes its objects as raw text: each object is converted to a string and the results are joined with ``sep``.
+
+It does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop text, render :ref:`console_markup`, or replace emoji codes. It does apply highlighting by default (set ``highlight=False`` to disable it), and it accepts a basic ``style`` argument. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("[bold]not markup[/bold]", ":smile:", {"a": 1})
+
